{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And to the wicked</b> — Because he began at first to contend with him, behold, he rebukes the devout, and now he speaks with a wise man who is wicked, for HaShem hates him, and this is the meaning of 'What right have you to recount My statutes' (when you do not keep them)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:28.274296020Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}